      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "When sorrow feels this heavy, the temptation to simply stop is overwhelming, but please recognize that the desire to cease the effort is the grief speaking, not necessarily your true self. While life involves loss, the process of grieving is about finding new reasons to connect and create meaning alongside that sadness. Giving yourself permission to feel tired is okay, but please allow yourself a small lifeline of professional care to help you explore ways through this heaviness.",
      "source": "target",
